.TH ISEKUR 1 "October 28, 2026" "iSekur 0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
isekur \- colorful terminal IRC client with a built-in webchat
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isekur
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-d | \-\-daemon ]
.RB [ \-a | \-\-attach ]
.RB [ \-\-web | \-\-no\-web ]
.RB [ \-\-hash\-password ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isekur
is a terminal IRC client with multiple servers and tabs, 24-bit color themes,
TLS, IRCv3 and SASL. Its optional webchat mirrors the running session in a
browser over HTTPS and WebSocket, so you can keep chatting from elsewhere.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file"
Use
.I file
instead of
.IR ~/.config/isekur/isekur.conf .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Start in the background without a terminal; attach with
.B \-\-attach
or the webchat, which this mode always tries to start (it needs
.B [web] user
and
.BR password_hash "). Output goes to"
.I isekur.log
next to the config file.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-attach
Bring a detached iSekur back to this terminal. Starting
.B isekur
while one is running with the same config does the same.
.TP
.BR \-\-web ", " \-\-no\-web
Start the webchat, or don't, regardless of
.B [web] autostart
(off by default). While running,
.B /web start
and
.B /web stop
do the same.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-password
Read a password and print a
.B [web] password_hash
line for the config.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Alt+1..9, Alt+0
Go to tab 1..10.
.TP
.B Alt+Left/Right, Ctrl+P/N
Previous / next tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A, Alt+A
Next tab with activity.
.TP
.B Alt+D
Detach (Option+D on a Mac): iSekur keeps running in the background, and
.B isekur \-\-attach
brings it back. Closing the terminal or a dropped SSH connection detaches too.
.TP
.B Ctrl+X
Next server.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close the tab.
.TP
.B PgUp, PgDn
Scroll.
.TP
.B Ctrl+L, Ctrl+T (or Alt+L, F2, Alt+T)
Show / hide the nicklist / the topic bar (Option+L, Option+T on a Mac).
.TP
.B F3
Toggle the mouse. With it on, a drag in the chat copies the text (OSC 52) and Shift+drag is the terminal's own selection; on the topic bar the wheel scrolls it, a click unfolds it and a double click edits it. Links in messages and the topic are terminal hyperlinks (OSC 8): Cmd+click or Ctrl+click opens them, with Shift when the terminal gives the click to iSekur. A right click on a server tab hides or shows its channels and queries in the tab bar (they stay reachable with Ctrl+N, Ctrl+P, Ctrl+A and /win). A right click on a channel tab opens a menu: quiet mode on or off, clear, add to or remove from autojoin, and close (it asks first when that leaves the channel). A right click on a nick in the nicklist opens a menu: query, whois, CTCP, ignore, and op, voice, kick and ban when your channel rank allows them.
.TP
.B Tab
Complete a command after \fB/\fR or \fB/help\fR, the config key after \fB/set\fR, or a nick (matches are listed as you type).
.TP
.B Home / End, Ctrl+E, Ctrl+U / Ctrl+K
Start / end of line, end of line, delete to start / end.
.TP
.B Alt+Backspace
Delete the previous word.
.TP
.B Cmd+Backspace
Delete to start, when the terminal forwards Cmd (CSI u).
.PP
Actions can be rebound in the
.B [keys]
section, also live with
.BR "/set keys.next_tab M\-n" .
.SH COMMANDS
.B /server host
.RB [ port "] [" \-tls "] [" \-noverify ],
.BR /connect ", " /disconnect ", " /join ", " /part ", " /msg ", " /query ,
.BR /me ", " /notice ", " /nick ", " /topic ", " /quiet ", " /close ", " /win " N, " /raw ,
.BR /ctcp ", " /theme ", " /set " [section.]key [value], " /save ", " /reload ,
.BR /ignore " [mask], " /unignore " mask, " /hilight " [add|del] word, " /grep " [-all] text, " /clear ", " /quit .
.B /e2e nick
asks for a password and starts an encrypted query with another iSekur user, who accepts with
.B /e2e
and your nick and the same password (AES-256-GCM, key from scrypt, kept in memory only);
.B /e2e off
ends it.
.B /e2e #channel
encrypts a channel for everyone who types the same password (no handshake; others see +iSE lines).
Channel operators also get
.BR /massop ", " /massdeop ", " /massvoice ", " /massdevoice ", " /masskick ,
.BR /lockdown ", " /unlock ", " /kickban " (" /kb "), " /tempban ", " /chanstats
and
.BR /topicrotate .
Other commands are sent to the server unchanged.
.B /help
lists them in the client;
.BI /help " command"
explains one, with examples.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/isekur/isekur.conf
Configuration (INI). Written with every setting on the first start; an empty value means the
default. See
.I iSekur.conf.example
in the data directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/isekur/themes/*.theme
User themes; also looked up in
.I ./themes
and the installed data directory.
.TP
.I <log_dir>/<server>/<name>.log
Chat logs when
.B log = on
is set; earlier days are kept as
.IR <name>.YYYY\-MM\-DD.log .
.TP
.I ~/.config/isekur/isekur.sock
The socket
.B \-\-attach
uses, only for your user. Its output in the background goes to
.I isekur.log
in the same directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/isekur/web.sessions
Hashed webchat login sessions.
